{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I'll be taking care of you during your stay. You came in with chest pain, nausea, and vomiting after dialysis yesterday. Can you tell me more about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, right after my dialysis session, I started feeling sick—nauseous, then vomiting. And this chest pain came on, like a thumping, going to my left shoulder. I felt dizzy too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any shortness of breath or fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or trouble breathing. Just the chest pain and nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We checked your heart enzymes and EKG. Your troponin was slightly elevated but stable, and the EKG changes look like they might be from lead placement, not a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not my heart again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It doesn’t look like a new heart attack. We’ll keep monitoring, but we think your symptoms may be from other causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also noticed two painful areas—one on your inner thigh and one on your left hip. They’re firm and discolored. Have they been getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they’ve been sore and hard. I thought it was cellulitis, so I’m on Bactrim."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re concerned it might be calciphylaxis, a condition where calcium builds up in the skin. We’ll do a CT scan and possibly a biopsy to confirm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Calciphylaxis? I’ve heard of that. Isn’t it serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, but we’re catching it early. We’ll start treatment if confirmed. Also, your urine test showed signs of infection—white blood cells and bacteria."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been having some burning when I pee. Could that be it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2118-11-27 16:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that fits. Since you have kidney disease, this is a complicated UTI. We’re starting IV antibiotics, then switching to oral cipro."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2118-11-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CT scan is back. It shows calcifications in your blood vessels and in the skin nodules on your thigh. This supports calciphylaxis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2118-11-28 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s confirmed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2118-11-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not fully. We’ll do a punch biopsy tomorrow to be sure. If positive, we’ll start sodium thiosulfate, which helps remove calcium from tissues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2118-11-28 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2118-11-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a small biopsy, done with local numbing. You’ll feel a pinch, but it’s quick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2118-11-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did the biopsy this morning. It confirmed calciphylaxis—calcium deposits in the small blood vessels of your skin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2118-11-29 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So what now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2118-11-29 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting sodium thiosulfate during dialysis. You’ll need daily dialysis for a week, then four times a week. This helps clear the calcium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2118-11-29 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Daily? That’s a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2118-11-29 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know. But it’s important to stop new lesions. We’ll adjust after your nephrologist sees you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2118-11-30 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m feeling nauseous again. Is it the new medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2118-11-30 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sodium thiosulfate can cause nausea. We’re also checking if your calcium acetate is contributing. We may switch to lanthanum."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2118-11-30 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had nausea with calcium acetate before. Maybe that’s it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2118-11-30 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you to lanthanum. We’ll also give you Zofran and Ativan for nausea as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2118-12-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been high—around 180s over 60s. We’re increasing your isosorbide dinitrate to 30 mg three times a day and starting amlodipine 5 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2118-12-01 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on blood pressure meds for years. Why’s it so hard to control?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2118-12-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "With kidney disease, it’s tougher. We’ll keep adjusting. You may need more changes after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2118-12-02 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My belly wound is still sore. Is it healing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2118-12-02 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Wound care checked it. They say it’s improving—good pink tissue, no infection. Keep following up with transplant surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2118-12-03 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are looking better. White count is down, kidney function stable. The antibiotics are working on your UTI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2118-12-03 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I haven’t had burning when I pee since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2118-12-03 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great sign. You’ll finish a 14-day course of cipro to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2118-12-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The sodium thiosulfate still makes me nauseous, but I can handle it if it helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2118-12-04 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m proud of you for sticking with it. We’ll keep managing the nausea. Dermatology will see you next week to check the lesions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2118-12-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Pain is controlled, nausea improved, and your wounds are stable. We’re planning discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2118-12-05 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Where will I go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2118-12-05 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "To an extended care facility for rehab and dialysis support. You’ll need help with daily dialysis four times a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2118-12-05 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2118-12-05 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue cipro for the UTI, lanthanum instead of calcium acetate, higher-dose blood pressure meds, and oxycodone for pain. Dilaudid for breakthrough pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2118-12-05 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the sodium thiosulfate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2118-12-05 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Three times a week during dialysis. We’ll coordinate with your outpatient team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2118-12-06 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous about managing all this at home later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2118-12-06 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. The rehab team will help you practice. You’ll have follow-ups with nephrology, dermatology, and transplant surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2118-12-06 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my chest pain hasn’t come back. That’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2118-12-06 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and your heart tests stayed stable. We think the nausea and UTI triggered the episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2118-12-06 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it wasn’t my heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2118-12-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do one more set of labs today. If they’re good, you’ll be discharged tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2118-12-06 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready to go, but I’ll miss the nurses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2118-12-06 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ve been great. You’ve made real progress—UTI clearing, pain controlled, and on track with calciphylaxis treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2118-12-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable. We’re ready to discharge you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2118-12-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What do I need to do next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2118-12-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Finish your cipro, keep up with four-times-weekly dialysis, and take sodium thiosulfate three times a week. Watch for new skin sores."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2118-12-07 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2118-12-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Dermatology in one week, transplant surgery for your wound, and your nephrologist to adjust dialysis and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2118-12-07 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2118-12-07 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep up the good work. Call if you have fever, worsening pain, or new symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2118-12-07 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave. How’s your pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s manageable. I used Dilaudid once yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Keep the oxycodone regular and Dilaudid as needed. And remember, no aspirin—we use Plavix instead due to your allergy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No aspirin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure is 187/62—still a bit high. Keep taking the new doses. We’ll follow up soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll watch it at the facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll help. And keep the wound clean. No soaking in baths."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. Stay on top of your appointments and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team will be here soon to take you to the extended care facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send all your records and prescriptions ahead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll be in touch with your outpatient team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Keep it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2118-12-07 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you soon in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2118-11-27 15:51:00",
    "admission_end": "2118-12-07 18:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with chest pain, nausea, and vomiting following a dialysis session. Initial concerns for cardiac ischemia were ruled out as troponin levels were mildly elevated but stable and MB negative, with EKG changes attributed to lead placement. A urinary tract infection was diagnosed based on urinalysis and symptoms of dysuria, and treated with cefepime initially, then transitioned to ciprofloxacin. Two painful skin lesions on the inner thigh and left hip were biopsied, confirming calciphylaxis, leading to initiation of sodium thiosulfate therapy and increased dialysis frequency to daily, then planned for four times weekly. Nausea was managed by switching from calcium acetate to lanthanum as a phosphate binder and using antiemetics. Hypertension was addressed with uptitration of isosorbide dinitrate and addition of amlodipine. The chronic abdominal wound showed signs of healing and was deemed stable. The patient was discharged to an extended care facility with plans for ongoing dialysis, dermatology follow-up, and management of multiple comorbidities.",
    "problems": [
      "Calciphylaxis",
      "Urinary tract infection",
      "Chronic, non-healing Abdominal wound",
      "HTN",
      "DM2",
      "CAD"
    ]
  }
}
